   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Five friendly letters",
     "texto": [
      "These five letters have a sound you already know in their basic pronunciation: **А** (a), **К** (k), **М** (m), **О** (o when it is stressed) and **Т** (t). Without stress, **О** is usually weakened and sounds like «a».",
      "With them you can already read **мама** (mum), **кот** (cat), **там** (there) and **как** (how)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Seven false friends",
     "texto": [
      "These look like letters you know from English, but they sound different. They are the trap of the first few days.",
      "**В** sounds **v**. **Н** sounds **n**. **Р** sounds **r**. **С** sounds **s**. **У** sounds **oo**. **Х** sounds like the **ch** in Scottish «loch».",
      "**Е** at the beginning of a word usually sounds like «ye»; after a consonant, it softens that consonant. That is why **нет** is closer to «nyet» than to «neet»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
